From a0fd073a263b7b08e0a606b3b53eb7a8475ecac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:10:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: complete IRIS1 legacy decoder buffer contract

SM8150 HFI4 legacy decoders rely on the split-output and extradata
contract used by Qualcomm msm/vidc and the Android OMX client. Align
VP8, VP9 and MPEG2 setup with that contract: use the real input
geometry, order and size DPB/OPB properties correctly, preserve HFI4
count_min_host, parse the HFI4 DPB-count event, and submit
firmware-sized DPB buffers.

Enable the default decoder extradata set and attach a private 16 KiB
DMA extradata buffer to every userspace capture buffer. Legacy sessions
use zero output tags and recover FBD and release-reference ownership by
packet-buffer address, matching downstream behavior without exposing
an extra V4L2 plane.

Validated on Xiaomi Raphael with Venus VP8 hardware decoding of 30
frames. Hardware and software NV12 output matched byte-for-byte at
13,824,000 bytes.

Signed-off-by: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
